Subject: [PATCH] wowbox64: GetEnvironmentVariableA ends the value with a NUL

wowbox64's GetEnvironmentVariableA (wine/common/wrt.c) copied the value with
RtlUnicodeToMultiByteN and wrote no closing NUL. Box64's Windows GetEnv (src/os/os_wine.c) reads
every variable into one static 1024-byte buffer, so a value kept the end of a longer value read
before it, and the last name of a BOX64_DYNAREC_PROGRAMS list (patch 0006) did not match. The
copy is now ended with a NUL when it leaves room for one.

Upstream: ptitSeb/box64 8851be9278e71b3bd608465836a34c2826ba7abb, "[WOWBOX64] Fixed
GetEnvironnementVariableA (for #4585)" (ptitSeb, 2026-10-22), the same change.
---
diff --git a/wine/common/wrt.c b/wine/common/wrt.c
--- a/wine/common/wrt.c
+++ b/wine/common/wrt.c
@@ -93,6 +93,7 @@ DWORD WINAPI GetEnvironmentVariableA(LPCSTR name, LPSTR value, DWORD size)
     else {
         ret = 0;
         if (len) RtlUnicodeToMultiByteN(value, size, &ret, valueW, len * sizeof(WCHAR));
+        if (ret < size) value[ret] = 0;
     }

     RtlFreeUnicodeString(&nameU);
